\begin{align*}
\left(\frac{x+5}{3}\right)^2+2=5 \quad &\Rightarrow \quad \left(\frac{x+5}{3}\right)^2=3\\
&\Rightarrow \quad \frac{x+5}{3}=\pm\sqrt{3}\\
&\Rightarrow \quad x+5=3(\pm\sqrt{3})\\
&\Rightarrow \quad x+5=\pm3\sqrt{3}\\
&\Rightarrow \quad x=-5\pm3\sqrt{3}\\
&\Rightarrow \quad x=-5-3\sqrt{3} \text{ or } x=-5+3\sqrt{3}
\end{align*}

Therefore, the solution is:
