generated_solution:
We first rewrite the expression as
\begin{align*}
(x^3 + xy^2 + yz^2)(y^3 + yx^2 + zx^2)(z^3 + zx^2 + xy^2) &= x^3 y^3 z^3 (1 + \frac{y^2}{x^2} + \frac{z^2}{x^2})(1 + \frac{x^2}{y^2} + \frac{z^2}{y^2})(1 + \frac{x^2}{z^2} + \frac{y^2}{z^2})\\
&= x^3 y^3 z^3 \left(1 + \frac{y^2}{x^2} + \frac{z^2}{x^2}\right) \left(1 + \frac{x^2}{y^2} + \frac{z^2}{y^2}\right) \left(1 + \frac{x^2}{z^2} + \frac{y^2}{z^2}\right).
\end{align*}
Now, we use the AM-GM inequality to obtain
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{3} \left(1 + \frac{y^2}{x^2} + \frac{z^2}{x^2}\right) &\ge \sqrt[3]{\frac{y^2 z^2}{x^4}}\\
\frac{1}{3} \left(1 + \frac{x^2}{y^2} + \frac{z^2}{y^2}\right) &\ge \sqrt[3]{\frac{x^2 z^2}{y^4}}\\
\frac{1}{3} \left(1 + \frac{x^2}{z^2} + \frac{y^2}{z^2}\right) &\ge \sqrt[3]{\frac{x^2 y^2}{z^4}}.
\end{align*}
Multiplying these three inequalities, we get
\[\frac{1}{27} \left(1 + \frac{y^2}{x^2} + \frac{z^2}{x^2}\right) \left(1 + \frac{x^2}{y^2} + \frac{z^2}{y^2}\right) \left(1 + \frac{x^2}{z^2} + \frac{y^2}{z^2}\right) \ge \sqrt[3]{\frac{x^2 y^2 z^2}{x^4 y^4 z^4}} = \frac{1}{xyz}.\]
This implies that
\begin{align*}
(x^3 + xy^2 + yz^2)(y^3 + yx^2 + zx^2)(z^3 + zx^2 + xy^2) &\le 27x^3 y^3 z^3 \cdot \frac{1}{xyz}\\
&= 27x^2 y^2 z^2.
\end{align*}
However, $x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 1$, so $x^2 y^2 z^2 \le \frac{1}{27}$, with equality if and only if $x = y = z = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}.$  Therefore, the maximum value is $\boxed{\frac{1}{27}}.$

