First, multiply the numerator and the denominator by $2+3i$:
\begin{align*}
\frac{(5+7i)}{(2-3i)} \cdot \frac{(2+3i)}{(2+3i)} &= \frac{(5+7i)(2+3i)}{(2-3i)(2+3i)} \\
&= \frac{10 + 15i + 14i + 21i^2}{2^2 - (3i)^2} \\
&= \frac{10 + 29i - 21}{4 + 9} \\
&= \frac{-11 + 29i}{13} \\
&= \boxed{-\frac{11}{13} + \frac{29}{13}i}
\end{align*}

