Using the given information and properties of cross products, we can simplify this expression:
   \begin{align*}
   \mathbf{a} \times 3 \mathbf{b} &= 3 \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = 3 \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 4 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 15 \\ 12 \\ -21 \end{pmatrix} \\
   \mathbf{a} \times 2 \mathbf{c} &= 2 \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c} = 2 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 2 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix} \\
